# Mova frontend — environment. Copy to services/frontend/.env.local (git-ignored) and fill in.
#
# The app runs against the hosted Supabase project; nothing needs to be installed for the database.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase → Project Settings → API. Public by design (they reach the browser), but ask for them with the rest.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY

# ── Heel Slide demo on your own machine ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run it with `npm run demo` (macOS, Linux and Windows). `npm run demo:check` checks this file by variable name and
# starts nothing.
#
# The one-press test sign-in buttons on /signin («Войти как тестовый пациент» / «Войти как тестовый врач»). They
# appear only on a development server (`npm run dev`, `npm run demo`) and on Vercel previews, never in a production
# build (`npm run build` + `npm start`). SECRETS: get them privately from Kassymzhomart; never commit or paste them.
HEEL_SLIDE_PATIENT_PASSWORD=
HEEL_SLIDE_CLINICIAN_PASSWORD=
# Only if the test accounts were seeded under other addresses (they must end in @mova.test):
# HEEL_SLIDE_PATIENT_EMAIL=heel-slide-patient@mova.test
# HEEL_SLIDE_CLINICIAN_EMAIL=heel-slide-clinician@mova.test
#
# Simulated sensors. `npm run demo` turns them on for that run only, so leave the flag out of this file. Without the
# script, put NEXT_PUBLIC_SENSOR_SIMULATION=1 (exactly "1") in .env.development.local, which only the development
# server reads, and restart it: NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are compiled in when it starts. Remove it before testing real
# sensors. Keep NEXT_PUBLIC_SENSOR_MOCK unset: with it on, «Далее» never opens.

# ── Not needed to run or present the app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Service-role key. Only scripts/seed-heel-slide.mjs reads it; the app never does. It bypasses every access rule on a
# database with real patients: never NEXT_PUBLIC_*, and a presenter's machine must not have it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# The deployment's own public origin, for sign-in redirects behind a proxy. Leave it unset locally: it overrides the
# browser's origin, so pinning it to localhost breaks sign-in from a phone on the same network.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://<your-app-host>
#
# Never set VERCEL_ENV in an env file (Vercel sets it itself). VERCEL_ENV=preview makes a production server show the
# test sign-in.
